(CEA-001 - Syrka Canonical Event Architecture) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Status: Accepted) Tj
T*
(Date: 2026-07-07) Tj
T*
(Builds on: ADR-001 - Selection of the Open-Source LMS Foundation for Syrka; ADR-002 - Syrka ) Tj
T*
(Domain Architecture, Bounded Contexts & System Ownership) Tj
T*
(Decision owners: Architecture / Platform Engineering / AI Engineering / Security) Tj
T*
(Scope: Canonical event language, envelope, taxonomy, event bus, event store, projections, ) Tj
T*
(connector mappings, AI consumption, security, privacy, versioning, testing, and governance) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Executive Overview) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Syrka is an event-driven Human Capital Infrastructure platform. Every meaningful business fact ) Tj
T*
(is represented as an immutable, canonical Syrka event. These events are the universal language ) Tj
T*
(used by the LMS boundary, identity, ontology, capability graph, inference engine, career ) Tj
T*
(engine, market intelligence, national vision layer, dashboards, passports, credentials, ) Tj
T*
(employers, governments, and cross-border workforce corridors.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The Canonical Event Architecture exists because Syrka must never be coupled to Open edX, ) Tj
T*
(Canvas, Moodle, Sakai, Chamilo, ILIAS, GitHub, LinkedIn, ORCID, OpenAlex, Semantic Scholar, an ) Tj
T*
(employer API, a government system, or any AI provider. External systems may produce signals. ) Tj
T*
(They do not define Syrka's facts.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Every subsystem communicates through canonical events rather than direct database access ) Tj
T*
(because:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Replaceability. Open edX can be replaced by Canvas, Moodle, a custom LMS, or a future ) Tj
T*
(platform by changing only the connector/anti-corruption layer.) Tj
T*
(2. Auditability. Events create a chronological, immutable record of what happened, who/what ) Tj
T*
(produced it, when it occurred, and which evidence supports it.) Tj
T*
(3. AI explainability. AI systems reason over canonical, provenance-rich evidence rather than ) Tj
T*
(opaque third-party schemas.) Tj
T*
(4. Domain ownership. Each bounded context owns its own model and projections. No service ) Tj
T*
(reaches into another service's database.) Tj
T*
(5. Replayability. Syrka can rebuild projections, dashboards, capability graph state, analytics,) Tj
T*
( passports, and recommendations from the event store.) Tj
T*
(6. Scalability. Producers and consumers evolve independently through versioned schemas and ) Tj
T*
(asynchronous delivery.) Tj
T*
(7. Compliance. Consent, privacy classification, retention, jurisdiction, and lineage travel ) Tj
T*
(with every event.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Events protect Syrka from LMS lock-in by turning LMS-specific activity into LMS-independent ) Tj
T*
(facts. For example, Open edX problem_check, Canvas quiz_submission, Moodle ) Tj
T*
(mod_quiz_attempt_submitted, and Sakai assessment submission events can all become canonical ) Tj
T*
(QuizCompleted or AssessmentSubmitted events. Downstream intelligence systems consume only the ) Tj
T*
(canonical event and therefore remain unchanged when the upstream LMS changes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Event Philosophy) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.1 Event) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(An event is an immutable record that something happened at a specific time. Events are append-) Tj
T*
(only. They are not updated. If a correction is required, a new correcting event is published.) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
endstream
