(2.2 Business Event) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A business event is an event that has domain meaning to Syrka. It describes a fact the business) Tj
T*
( cares about, such as AssignmentSubmitted, CapabilityObserved, PassportIssued, or ) Tj
T*
(EmployerInterested.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.3 Canonical Event) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A canonical event is a business event expressed in Syrka's platform-independent language, ) Tj
T*
(envelope, schema, privacy model, and versioning rules. Canonical events are independent of any ) Tj
T*
(source system's internal event names or database schemas.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.4 Observation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(An observation is a captured signal that may indicate a capability, behavior, preference, risk,) Tj
T*
( or market condition. Observations are not necessarily conclusions. CommitObserved, ) Tj
T*
(AttendanceRecorded, and DiscussionParticipated are observations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.5 Evidence) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Evidence is an observation, artifact, assessment, credential, or verified external signal that ) Tj
T*
(can support a claim. Evidence must have provenance and must be referenceable. Evidence may be ) Tj
T*
(strong, weak, conflicting, stale, or revoked.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.6 Provenance) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Provenance describes where an event came from, which system produced it, which source ) Tj
T*
(record/artifact it references, what adapter/model version transformed it, and how it can be ) Tj
T*
(verified or replayed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.7 Fact) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A fact is a canonical event accepted by the event platform after validation. A fact may later ) Tj
T*
(be superseded or corrected, but the original fact remains part of the audit history.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.8 Projection) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A projection is derived state built from events. Examples include a student's current ) Tj
T*
(capability summary, an institutional dashboard aggregate, or a passport read model. Projections) Tj
T*
( are rebuildable.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.9 Read Model) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A read model is an optimized query representation of one or more projections. Read models are ) Tj
T*
(built for product surfaces and analytics. They are not sources of truth.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.10 Distinctions) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(| Concept | Source of truth? | Mutable? | Example | Notes |) Tj
T*
(|---|---:|---:|---|---|) Tj
T*
(| Event | Yes, for the fact it records | No | AssignmentSubmitted | Append-only |) Tj
T*
(| Observation | Yes, for observed signal | No | CommitObserved | May support inference |) Tj
T*
(| Evidence | Yes, as support for claims | No or revocable by new event | Submission artifact | Linked to ) Tj
T*
(provenance |) Tj
ET
endstream
