(Every event schema must define:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Purpose - why the event exists.) Tj
T*
(2. Business meaning - the fact it records.) Tj
T*
(3. Producer - exactly one canonical producer domain.) Tj
T*
(4. Consumers - primary expected consumers.) Tj
T*
(5. Required fields - payload fields required in addition to the universal envelope.) Tj
T*
(6. Optional fields - additive payload fields.) Tj
T*
(7. Validation rules - schema, domain, authorization, and referential checks.) Tj
T*
(8. Privacy classification - public/internal/restricted/highly restricted.) Tj
T*
(9. Security requirements - signing, encryption, scopes, tenant boundaries.) Tj
T*
(10. Versioning rules - compatibility and migration requirements.) Tj
T*
(11. Retention policy - short/standard/long/permanent/jurisdictional.) Tj
T*
(12. Replay policy - whether replay is safe, constrained, or forbidden.) Tj
T*
(13. Example payload - canonical JSON example.) Tj
T*
(14. Failure handling - validation, retry, DLQ, quarantine.) Tj
T*
(15. Idempotency strategy - deterministic keys and duplicate handling.) Tj
T*
(16. Ordering guarantees - partition key and expected order.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5.2 Default validation rules) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Envelope validates against the universal JSON Schema.) Tj
T*
(- event_type must match the schema name.) Tj
T*
(- event_version must be registered.) Tj
T*
(- tenant_id, source_system, producer, occurred_at, and idempotency_key are required.) Tj
T*
(- actor, subject, and resource must use canonical ID formats where applicable.) Tj
T*
(- Required payload fields must be present and type-valid.) Tj
T*
(- Payload must not contain raw secrets, passwords, tokens, or unclassified large artifacts.) Tj
T*
(- Evidence artifacts must be referenced through secure evidence_refs, not embedded.) Tj
T*
(- Events from connectors must include source provenance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5.3 Default privacy classifications) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(| Classification | Meaning | Examples | Handling |) Tj
T*
(|---|---|---|---|) Tj
T*
(| public | Intended for public disclosure | published public profile event | signed; no sensitive data |) Tj
T*
(| internal | Syrka internal operational data | schema published, market aggregate | tenant-aware access |) Tj
T*
(| restricted | Personal, institutional, or business-sensitive | course progress, job matches | encrypted, scoped ) Tj
T*
(authorization |) Tj
T*
(| highly_restricted | High-impact personal/evidence data | grades, passport, consent, mobility | strict ) Tj
T*
(authorization, audit, minimization |) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
