(10.4 Partitions and ordering) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Partition by stable business key, not random event ID. Partition keys are defined in section ) Tj
T*
(5.6. Global ordering is not guaranteed and must not be required.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(10.5 Delivery semantics) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Syrka uses at-least-once delivery with idempotent producers and consumers. Exactly-once end-to-) Tj
T*
(end delivery is not assumed. Exactly-once-like behavior is implemented through idempotency ) Tj
T*
(keys, transactional outbox, consumer checkpoints, and deterministic projections.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(10.6 Retry and back-pressure) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Use exponential backoff with jitter.) Tj
T*
(- Use bounded retries before DLQ.) Tj
T*
(- Consumers must expose lag metrics.) Tj
T*
(- Producers must support back-pressure and circuit breakers.) Tj
T*
(- High-volume analytics events may be sampled only if explicitly declared and not used as ) Tj
