(13.2 Stages) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Evidence extraction. Extract text, metadata, rubric scores, code metrics, citations, or ) Tj
T*
(artifacts from evidence references.) Tj
T*
(2. Normalization. Convert raw evidence into feature records with source event IDs.) Tj
T*
(3. Ontology mapping. Match evidence to skills, knowledge, occupations, and capabilities using ) Tj
T*
(ontology version metadata.) Tj
T*
(4. Retrieval. Pull relevant graph context, prior evidence, rubric definitions, and market ) Tj
T*
(signals.) Tj
T*
(5. Inference. Apply deterministic rules, statistical models, and LLM reasoning through provider) Tj
T*
( adapters.) Tj
T*
(6. Confidence scoring. Combine evidence quality, recency, difficulty, assessor trust, model ) Tj
T*
(uncertainty, and corroboration.) Tj
T*
(7. Explainability. Generate evidence-linked explanations and limitations.) Tj
T*
(8. Policy and bias checks. Apply fairness, safety, and high-impact decision gates.) Tj
T*
(9. Publication. Publish CapabilityObserved, RecommendationGenerated, or review events.) Tj
T*
(10. Feedback loop. Consume user/faculty/employer feedback as new events.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
